        <div class="figure-caption">
          <h3>Topology growth observation</h3>
          <p>
            As the number of federation links grows, candidate certification paths
            increase and exhaustive exploration becomes less manageable.
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="research-card">
        <div class="research-card-header">
          <h3>Weighted path selection</h3>
        </div>
        <p>
          The proposal introduces a multicriteria weighting function over federation
          edges to prioritize cryptographic robustness, compatibility, and structural
          efficiency during certification path selection.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Edge weights capture algorithm, crypto profile, key strength, and logical distance.</li>
          <li>Dijkstra is proposed to compute deterministic optimal paths over the graph.</li>
          <li>The target is explainable route selection between issuer CA and governed trust points.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </div>

    <div class="research-notes">
      <div>
        <span class="note-label">Research problem</span>
        <p>
          Exhaustive trust-path discovery does not scale well in dense multidomain PKI federations.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <span class="note-label">Methodological lens</span>
        <p>
          Directed weighted graphs, Dijkstra traversal, and policy-aware trust modelling.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div id="interoperability">
        <span class="note-label">Interoperability objective</span>
        <p>
          Support controlled interoperability across classical, hybrid, and post-quantum PKI domains.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
